This script takes the simulation data and then convert them to mimic real data to run through the eventcleaning

to just run the script locally on a single file 
./run_script.sh <YYYYMMDD> <SIMRUN> [GROPT|CARE] [runFolder]
./run_script.sh 20260901 tausofia CARE
./run_script.sh 20260803 muonkiet CARE
./run_script.sh 20260413 16190401_daro GROPT
./run_script.sh 20260916 nathanwmycare CARE job_000004   <- one run folder only

./run_all this will run all on the local node (slow)

<YYYYMMDD>_<SIMRUN> names a folder under simdata/<daviddata|sofiadata>/ and two
layouts are handled automatically:

  flat      <YYYYMMDD>_<SIMRUN>/<stage>/Tilt_*/*.root
  campaign  <YYYYMMDD>_<SIMRUN>/<YYYYMMDD_RUN_xx>/<stage>/Tilt_*/*.root

The newer sofia productions are the campaign form, e.g.
simdata/sofiadata/20260901_tausofia/20260901_10455802_ss/CARE/Tilt_90.000000/,
so one call walks every run folder underneath the campaign and writes them all
into a single set of outputs named after the campaign. Run folders that are
still producing, or that have no ISOG file yet, are reported and skipped, so the
finished part of a night can be analysed while the rest is running. The tilt
folder is matched on its "Tilt_" prefix, so the tilt angle does not have to be
known in advance.

ISOG columns
------------
The shower information is matched to the events by row number: ISOG row N
describes tree entry N (checked to hold on all 58 run folders of 20260916 -
715 rows against 715 entries, and so on). SimRootFiles now verifies both halves
of that before reading a run: the column names in the ISOG header have to be the
ones it assigns to the SEvent, and the row count has to equal the tree entry
count. A run that fails either check is skipped rather than written out with
shower parameters sitting on the wrong events.

The 22 stored columns are, in order:
  PolarAngle AzimuthAngle XTel YTel ZTel TelescopeRadius XMax NMax X0 Lambda
  NeutrinoEnergy DecayLength ShowerStartX ShowerStartY ShowerStartZ
  TauEmergenceProb EmergencePointX EmergencePointY EmergencePointZ
  GlobeTheta GlobePhi TauEnergy
ISOG also writes PExit, LastSurfaceCode, RunCHASMFlag and MasterSeed after
those; SEvent has no field for them, and MasterSeed is a 128 bit integer that
would not fit a Float_t anyway.

ISOG writes "nan" for a column that does not apply to a shower - ShowerStartX/Y/Z
on anything that never decayed. Reading the row with "iss >> Float_t" stopped
dead on that token and left every later column unset, which is why tau energy
came back missing on 20260916: the first nan is column 12, so only 12 of the 26
columns were ever read. The row is now converted one token at a time, so a nan
stays in its own column.

Each event records the run folder it came from in the Sim tree (SimRun), and
the histogram/canvas keys in plots_*.root are named
h_<date>_<run folder>_<event> so they stay unique across the campaign.

the 4th argument of SimRootFiles picks which simulation stage to read.
GROPT (the default) reads the ray traced photons out of T1 and makes the
1mm / 6mm camera views. CARE reads the FADC traces out of Events/T0 and
makes the 16x16 PE camera view from the sample at timebin 25. Both read the
same ISOG row for a shower, so the event label, the Sim tree and the Test
tree carry the same information either way. Each stage
writes into its own folder, data/<date>/<GROPT|CARE>/, so the two do not
overwrite each other.

to recompile 
./compile_script.sh

-------------------------------------------------
CONDOR - one job per run folder

A campaign is far too much for one node: 20260916_nathanwmycare is 58 run
folders and about 42000 showers between them. Each run folder is self contained
though - its own GROPT/CARE files and its own ISOG file describing the same
showers - so they parallelise with no merging of shower information needed.

    ./submit_sim.sh <YYYYMMDD> <SIMRUN> [GROPT|CARE]
    ./submit_sim.sh 20260916 nathanwmycare CARE

submit_sim.sh walks the campaign, writes the run folders that actually have both
a stage folder with .root files and an ISOG .txt to
condor_lists/run_folders_<date>_<simrun>_<simtype>.txt, and submits one job per
line. Folders still being produced are reported and left out rather than queued
for a job that would only skip them on the node. Run with DRYRUN=1 to write the
list and print the submit command without submitting.

    plotcamera.submit    one job per run folder, queued from that list
    run_condor_sim.sh    runs inside the job: rebuilds the directory tree that
                         SimRootFiles expects out of the flat transferred
                         inputs, then runs it for that one run folder

Only that run folder's stage and ISOG directories are transferred, not the whole
campaign. Note a CARE folder carries its .vbf along with the .root, about 30 MB
per job.

Every output file is named with the run folder in it,
datafiles_<date>_<simrun>_<runFolder>.root, so the jobs all write into the
shared data/<date>/<simtype>/ without overwriting each other. To get back the
single tree a local pass produces:

    ./merge_sim_output.sh <YYYYMMDD> <SIMRUN> [GROPT|CARE]

which hadds them into datafiles_<date>_<simrun>.root and leaves the per run
folder files in place.

To reproduce one failed job by hand, give run_script.sh the same run folder the
job got:  ./run_script.sh 20260916 nathanwmycare CARE job_000004

ISOG columns are dumped per shower when ISOGVERBOSE=1 is set; it is off by
default because 22 lines an event would bury the condor log.

-------------------------------------------------
CONDOR - the older flat layout (still here, unchanged)
create the file that has all sim files to run over 
./get_folders_tocsv.sh 
then 
condor_submit convertsim2data.submit
    uses ./run_condor.sh for inside the job
NOTE: this path assumes the old flat GROPT/Tilt_91.560000 layout (see
run_condor.sh and the transfer_input_files line in the submit file); use
submit_sim.sh above for campaign folders.















-------------------------------------------------
HIVE how to run
how to run

./SimRootFiles YYYYMMDD SIMRUN MOUNT [GROPT|CARE] [runFolder]
samples
./SimRootFiles 20250529 Tilt_91.560000 y
./SimRootFiles 20250529 Tilt_91.560000 y CARE
./SimRootFiles 20260901 tausofia y CARE
./SimRootFiles 20260916 nathanwmycare y CARE job_000004
